## 4. Phase 3 — Final verification

```bash
oc get nodes -o wide                                   # 3 masters Ready
oc get machines,bmh -n openshift-machine-api           # all 3 machines Running, BMH consumers set
oc rsh -n openshift-etcd etcd-master03.3novvt.samsungcnfcu.local etcdctl member list -w table     # 3 started
oc rsh -n openshift-etcd etcd-master03.3novvt.samsungcnfcu.local etcdctl endpoint health --cluster
oc get co etcd kube-apiserver kube-controller-manager kube-scheduler   # DEGRADED False on all
oc get co                                               # nothing Degraded / Progressing
oc get mcp master                                       # 3/3 ready, not degraded
oc get clusterversion                                   # Progressing False
oc adm wait-for-stable-cluster --minimum-stable-period=5m
```

Load balancer: re-enable master01 and master02 in HAProxy backends for **6443** and **22623** (and 80/443 if ingress is on masters). Confirm health checks are green:

```bash
echo "show stat" | sudo socat stdio /var/run/haproxy/admin.sock | grep -E 'master0[12]'
```

Data-loss check: because quorum was rebuilt from one member's local data, writes in flight at the moment of failure can be missing. Spot-check anything created/changed in the last ~10 minutes before the outage (deployments, secrets, routes, PVCs) and re-apply from Git/CI if needed.

Fresh backup after recovery:

```bash
oc debug node/master03.3novvt.samsungcnfcu.local -- chroot /host /usr/local/bin/cluster-backup.sh /home/core/assets/backup
```

