## 5. Troubleshooting

| Symptom | Likely cause | Action |
|---|---|---|
| `quorum-restore.sh` exits with error about etcd container | Script needs the etcd static pod present | `sudo crictl ps -a \| grep etcd`; check `/etc/kubernetes/manifests/etcd-pod.yaml` exists; rerun with `sudo -E`. |
| API still read-only / timeouts 10 min after script | etcd came up but kube-apiserver not restarted | On master03: `sudo crictl ps \| grep kube-apiserver`; if absent, `sudo systemctl restart kubelet`. |
| Rebuilt node Ready but etcd stays at previous member count | Leftover `etcd-*-<node>` secret, or node name differs from FQDN | Re-run §3.1 secret deletion; compare `oc get nodes` name with BMH/keyfile hostname; check `oc logs -n openshift-etcd-operator deploy/etcd-operator`. |
| etcd operator idle, no new revision | Rollout not triggered | `oc patch etcd cluster -p='{"spec":{"forceRedeploymentReason":"recovery-'"$(date --rfc-3339=ns)"'"}}' --type=merge` |
| Rebuilt node stuck fetching ignition (22623) | Route/DNS/LB | From live ISO shell: `curl -kI https://api-int.3novvt.samsungcnfcu.local:22623/healthz`; verify HAProxy backend master03 is UP for 22623. |
| No CSRs appear for the new node | Node cannot reach 6443, or Machine object missing | Verify §3.2 Machine exists; `curl -k https://api-int…:6443/healthz` from the node console. |
| Machine stays `Provisioning` after node is Ready | Node not linked to BMH (MAC mismatch) | Compare node MAC/IP with `bmh.spec.bootMACAddress`; patch and wait. |
| kube-apiserver `NodeInstallerDegraded` for a while | Static-pod revisions rolling out | Normal; wait for installer pods in `openshift-kube-apiserver` to complete. |
| A failed node was accidentally powered on with its old disk | Old member tries to rejoin old cluster ID | Power it off immediately; it will be rejected anyway (cluster ID changed) but must be reinstalled from ISO — never let its old etcd data rejoin. |

